and in two ways the plan was pleasing to them,
either to sack-through or in two parts all to share
the property, as much as the lovely citadel held within;

and golden clothes the two wore,
fine and great in their armour, as gods indeed,
conspicuous apart;

And among them Strife, and among them Uproar, kept thronging, and among them baleful Death-spirit,
holding one man alive, newly wounded, another unwounded,
and another, dead, she was dragging through the press by the feet;

And whenever, having turned, they came to the boundary of the field,
then into their hands a cup of honey-sweet wine
would a man give, coming up to them;

And three sheaf-binders stood by; and behind
boys, gathering handfuls, in armfuls bearing them,
unceasingly supplied them;

And among them in the midst a boy on a clear-sounding lyre
was playing, full of longing, and the Linos-song beneath it beautifully he sang
in a slender voice;

And these at one time would run on knowing feet
very easily, as when a wheel fitted in his hands
a potter, sitting, will try, whether it will run;
